     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't change the pharmacology. A single 4,000 mg dose of ibuprofen is in the range associated with significant toxicity, and 16,000 mg/day could seriously harm your patient. Order entry would also be the last safeguard before it reached the patient.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range**, such as 800 mg by mouth four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum) or 400 mg four times daily.\n- **Enter it with a note** asking pharmacy to verify, if you have a clinical rationale I'm not aware of. I'd still need a dose I can safely place.\n- **Help with a different goal.** If you're trying to get stronger analgesia or anti-inflammatory effect, I can enter a multimodal regimen, such as scheduled acetaminophen plus ibuprofen at the maximum dose.\n\nTell me which you'd like, and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
